{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bjlxdnjs8","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FwZfzHmFXJRvAji1LHB6q6","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/d146f9e5-483a-4621-b4a6-581ee9833faf/tasks/bjlxdnjs8.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `personal_lapse_ideal_alternation`: each person still judges a sequence as more random the closer its proportion of alternations lies to their own personal ideal switching rate, and still guesses on some trials at a personal, trait-like lapse rate, but people also treat a long streak of identical flips as a sign of non-randomness, and how strongly a streak puts them off is each person's own trait (a personal weight on the longest run relative to sequence length, drawn from a population). The one change is this individual streak-aversion weight, added because the critique shows participants differ in their preference for the sequence with the shorter longest run more than the model's alternation, balance and lapse heterogeneity produces, and that streaks are penalised beyond alternation among alternation-matched pairs.\nEOF\necho lapse_individual_streak_aversion > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/candidate.py\n\"\"\"Personal lapse rate on a personal-ideal-alternation judgment with individual streak aversion.\n\nRefinement of `personal_lapse_ideal_alternation`: each person judges a sequence\nas more random the closer its alternation rate lies to their own ideal\nswitching rate, and guesses on some trials at a personal lapse rate. The one\nchange: a long streak of identical flips makes a sequence look less random, by\na weight on the longest run (relative to sequence length) that is each\nperson's own, drawn from a population distribution.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pymc as pm\nimport pytensor.tensor as pt\n\nMAX_PARTICIPANTS = 400\n\n\ndef compute_features(sequence_a, sequence_b):\n    def alternation_rate(seq):\n        if len(seq) < 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"sequence too short: {seq!r}\")\n        return sum(1 for x, y in zip(seq, seq[1:]) if x != y) / (len(seq) - 1)\n\n    def longest_run(seq):\n        best = cur = 1\n        for x, y in zip(seq, seq[1:]):\n            cur = cur + 1 if x == y else 1\n            best = max(best, cur)\n        return best / len(seq)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()\n    b = sequence_b.strip().upper()\n    return {\n        \"alt_rate_a\": alternation_rate(a),\n        \"alt_rate_b\": alternation_rate(b),\n        \"max_run_a\": longest_run(a),\n        \"max_run_b\": longest_run(b),\n    }\n\n\nwith pm.Model() as model:\n    alt_rate_a = pm.Data(\"alt_rate_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    alt_rate_b = pm.Data(\"alt_rate_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    max_run_a = pm.Data(\"max_run_a\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    max_run_b = pm.Data(\"max_run_b\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n\n    # Personal ideal alternation rate (non-centred logit-normal population).\n    mu_ideal = pm.Normal(\"mu_ideal\", mu=0.4, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_ideal = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_ideal\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_ideal = pm.Normal(\"z_ideal\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    ideal = pm.Deterministic(\"ideal\", pm.math.sigmoid(mu_ideal + sigma_ideal * z_ideal))\n    # Sensitivity to squared distance from the ideal.\n    beta = pm.LogNormal(\"beta\", mu=2.5, sigma=0.5)\n\n    # Personal streak-aversion weight on relative longest run (non-centred normal).\n    mu_delta = pm.Normal(\"mu_delta\", mu=0.0, sigma=2.0)\n    sigma_delta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_delta\", sigma=1.5)\n    z_delta = pm.Normal(\"z_delta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    delta = mu_delta + sigma_delta * z_delta\n\n    # Personal lapse (guessing) rate (non-centred logit-normal population).\n    mu_lapse = pm.Normal(\"mu_lapse\", mu=-2.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_lapse = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_lapse\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_lapse = pm.Normal(\"z_lapse\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    lapse = pm.Deterministic(\"lapse\", pm.math.sigmoid(mu_lapse + sigma_lapse * z_lapse))\n\n    theta = ideal[participant_id]\n    d = delta[participant_id]\n    score_a = -beta * pt.sqr(alt_rate_a - theta) - d * max_run_a\n    score_b = -beta * pt.sqr(alt_rate_b - theta) - d * max_run_b\n    p_engaged = pm.math.sigmoid(score_a - score_b)\n    lam = lapse[participant_id]\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\", pt.clip(0.5 * lam + (1.0 - lam) * p_engaged, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    )\n\n    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"int64\"))\n    pm.Bernoulli(\"response\", p=p_left, observed=chose_left)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"3f80f29f-af62-4a65-be1e-fcdc387cb3eb","session_id":"d146f9e5-483a-4621-b4a6-581ee9833faf"}
