{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaCz9Ubm3N67u8nYw7j2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate and it passes the admission self-check: `check_candidate` printed `OK`. That was only a short smoke fit (100 draws, one chain), so convergence and novelty weren't checked, and its PSIS-LOO came out unreliable (6.3% of trials had high Pareto-k, against a 1% tolerance).\n\n**Model chosen: `personal_lapse_ideal_alternation`**, the best live model after the incumbent. It keeps the personal ideal switching rate and the personal lapse (guessing) rate.\n\n**The one change:** each person also gets their own weight against long streaks. The model computes the longest run of identical flips, divided by the sequence's length, and each participant has their own weight on it, drawn from a population distribution. This goes after the critique's two streak findings: people differ in streak aversion more than the incumbent produces, and among pairs with similar alternation rates they avoid the sequence with a streak at its start or end. Neither survived the FDR correction (both q = 0.12).\n\nThis is also a real alternative to the incumbent. Both add a per-person second cue to the lapse model, but the incumbent's cue is heads/tails balance and this one's is streak length.\n\n**Smoke-fit result:** ELPD-LOO of −943.6, against the incumbent's −952.4 from its full fit. That looks promising, but it comes from a smoke fit with an unreliable LOO estimate, so it doesn't show the model is better. Admission's full fit will decide.\n\n- **Name:** `lapse_individual_streak_aversion`\n- **Files** (all in `iter_4/candidate_5/`): `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt`, `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3225,"cache_read_input_tokens":65371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3225,"ephemeral_1h_inpu